Third-party / upstream fixtures
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bundled RPMs, SRPMs, buildroots, and related archives retain their upstream
licenses and copyright notices. They are not relicensed under the Apache
License 2.0 solely by virtue of the root LICENSE file.

Notable paths:

- gather-rpms.tar.gz — Fedora mock buildroots for a real build of the `at`
  package (see README for how the archive was produced). Package contents
  remain under their Fedora/upstream terms.
- broken-noarch-subpackage/ and valid-noarch-subpackage/ — test SRPMs and
  binary RPMs used by noarch checks; retain upstream packaging licenses.
- pytest-rpms/ — Fedora pytest package RPMs/SRPMs; retain upstream terms.
- git-repos/ — archived git trees used as test inputs; contents retain any
  upstream licenses present in those trees.
